","format":"PNG","original":"radia_s15_n159_radiox_schreiner.mp3","mtime":"1493458111","size":"10450","md5":"5d507498e02e30956e5f5f67c5288f42","crc32":"9453d2b8","sha1":"f259070211ffe0a8e595a2ad7de653a149f9e6e0"},{"name":"radia_s15_n159_radiox_schreiner_archive.torrent","source":"metadata","btih":"71c59dfdb92d04dbdf0f6f70f0232cfb0b1cfc47","mtime":"1554960283","size":"5346","md5":"be5ca926a3ed3f74f432ffac0e42a78f","crc32":"9037e780","sha1":"52f4a32516c93fd973ce3ec2097daa98b994dcb4","format":"Archive BitTorrent"},{"name":"radia_s15_n159_radiox_schreiner_files.xml","source":"original","format":"Metadata","md5":"d3e1ba6d4aba298cf9ecb3142caac260","summation":"md5"},{"name":"radia_s15_n159_radiox_schreiner_meta.sqlite","source":"original","mtime":"1493457975","size":"22528","format":"Metadata","md5":"36f0978cd7d368348e1c9bf88913d5cc","crc32":"4563bfc3","sha1":"22bcd85e5f4e9299cc2923c9e6eaacf754e505a7"},{"name":"radia_s15_n159_radiox_schreiner_meta.xml","source":"original","mtime":"1667679702","size":"2627","format":"Metadata","md5":"584b67b2cf9f8bc1c761cdf279ce9ac3","crc32":"92d0fd08","sha1":"875db26feff43769a71fd16fb501c2046eb69d09"}],"files_count":11,"item_last_updated":1667679702,"item_size":64215916,"metadata":{"identifier":"radia_s15_n159_radiox_schreiner","mediatype":"audio","collection":["radiafm","radioprograms","radiostationarchives"],"description":"<div class=\"entry-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Untitled (Two Channel Piece Hamburg) by Bernhard Schreiner is \nbased on a  sound art piece performed live at Pudel Club Hamburg in June\n 2007,  edited for radiator x/radia art radio network in 2008.</p>\n<p>The alternative title in brackets relates to the fact that the two  \nchannel piece is kind of special in so far as Schreiner’s sound  \nperformances and sculptures are usually four channel pieces.</p>\n<p>Bernhard Schreiner (* 1971, A) works with film, video and sound.  \nExploring the materiality of his media, he is creating visual  \nnoise/music from 16mm film and builiding sculptural assemblage as well  \nas whole environments based on sound.<br />\nFrom 1991 to 1998 Schreiner studied at the Staedelschule Academy  \nFrankfurt am Main (Peter Kubelka). In addition to his own artistic work \n he is regularly curating projects in the fields of experimental film \nand  sound art, a. o. the Environmental Sound Matter series for \nSteirischer  Herbst & musikprotokoll Graz 2007 and 2008. In 2004, he\n founded the  sound art label feld records (www.feld-records.com).<br />\nHis films are distributed by independent media art distributions like  \nsixpackfilm (www.sixpackfilm.com); for more info see also the Austrian  \nIndependent Film and Video Database (filmvideo.at).<br />\nCurrently he lives in Frankfurt am Main and Berlin (Germany).</p>\n<p>This show was created for radiator x  (radio art @ radio x frankfurt \nam main in coop. with radia art radio  network), ed. Verena Kuni.<br />\nFor more info see: www.gunst.info/radiator and www.radiox.de</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>","licenseurl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/3.0/","radiaseason":"15","scanner":"Internet Archive HTML5 Uploader 1.6.3","subject":"radio art;Radia;radio x","title":"Show 0159: Untitled (Two Channel Piece Hamburg) by Bernhard Schreiner (radio x)","publicdate":"2017-04-29 09:24:55","uploader":"radia.fm@gmail.com","addeddate":"2017-04-29 09:24:55","creator":"radio x","date":"2008-04-14","backup_location":"ia906403_6","external_metadata_update":"2019-04-11T05:24:32Z"},"server":"ia601501.us.archive.org","uniq":1957449856,"workable_servers":["ia601501.us.archive.org","ia801501.us.archive.org"]}